    "note": "Source: the W3C Working Group's own publication snapshot of the Recommendation, github.com/w3c/json-ld-syntax at commit 029777cff904bfa59cfdfc19e2c6c6098e33ef60, path publication-snapshots/REC/Overview.html (last changed there in a97d1d26648fea976298026a90e571f20ba889b7, 2020-07-07). Its status section and header read 'W3C Recommendation 16 July 2020', 'This version: https://www.w3.org/TR/2020/REC-json-ld11-20200716/'. It is therefore the REC text as the WG staged it for publication, NOT an editor's draft; w3.org is unreachable from the ingesting container, so it was not compared byte for byte with the copy at https://www.w3.org/TR/2020/REC-json-ld11-20200716/. Printed to PDF offline (headless Chromium 141, network blocked, document outline from the headings), then ingested with the pdf-structure rung. Styles and the W3C logo, which load from w3.org, are absent from the print; the text and the repository-local figures are not. Errata published after the REC are not included. NOTICE: This entry includes material copied from or derived from JSON-LD 1.1, https://www.w3.org/TR/2020/REC-json-ld11-20200716/. Copyright © 2010-2020 W3C® (MIT, ERCIM, Keio, Beihang). Licensed under the W3C Software and Document License, https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/2015/copyright-software-and-document. Changes: the HTML was printed to PDF and its text split into one Markdown file per outline section; the wording is unchanged."
